---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Questions from '../components/Questions.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import headshot from '../assets/headshot.webp';
---

<Base>
  <section class="intro">
    <Image
      src={headshot}
      alt={`Portrait of ${site.name}`}
      width={240}
      densities={[1, 2]}
      loading="eager"
      class="portrait"
    />
    <div>
      <h1>{site.name}</h1>
      <p class="role">{site.role}<br /><span class="muted">{site.org}</span></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <p class="lede">Hellenic by birth. Texan by choice. Architect by discipline.</p>

  <p>Three things I’ve learned in two decades of leading technology in higher education:</p>
  <ul class="lessons">
    <li>The campus closest to the problem usually has the best answer. Listen first.</li>
    <li>AI will not replace judgment. It will expose whether you had any.</li>
    <li>The point of architecture is not to be admired. It is to be load-bearing.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Before The Texas A&amp;M University System, I spent seven years as CTO and Deputy CIO at UT San
    Antonio, where the work that mattered most was the work nobody noticed. I am also a Ph.D.
    candidate in Cybersecurity and AI at UTSA. <a href="/experience/">Experience →</a>
  </p>

  <h2>Questions I work on</h2>
  <Questions />
  <p class="more"><a href="/research/">Research →</a></p>

  <h2>Why limur</h2>
  <p>
    <em>Limur</em> is short for <strong>less is more</strong>: fewer systems, clearer boundaries,
    decisions you can explain. It is also the name of my research on LLM-driven cybersecurity
    playbooks.
  </p>
</Base>

<style>
  .intro {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .portrait {
    width: 7.5rem;
    height: 7.5rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: 50% 25%;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .intro h1 {
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }

  .role {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .lessons {
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }

  .lessons li {
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }

  .more {
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 30rem) {
    .intro {
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: flex-start;
    }
  }
</style>
